# Why Do We Need Joins?

Imagine Swiggy.

Customer information is stored separately.

Orders are stored separately.

Menu items are stored separately.

Payments are stored separately.

Instead of storing everything in one table:

```text
Customer
   |
Orders
   |
Products
```

SQL uses JOINs to combine data from multiple tables.

